# HTTP webserver benchmark matrix (mandatory)

After **every** li-httpd implementation step (runtime, packages, tier-5 scenario, or catalog row):

## 1. Run tier-5 throughput (all scenarios)

```bash
cd benchmarks
export LIC_ROOT=/path/to/lic   # epoll checkout for real RPS; main stub = static only
export LI_HTTPD_BIN="$LIC_ROOT/build/li-httpd"
export BENCH_HTTP_PROFILE=nightly
export BENCH_HTTP_ORACLES=nginx,apache,lighttpd,node,bun,li
./scripts/run-tier5-http-bench.sh
./scripts/benchmark-matrix-report.py
```

Optional supplemental proxy row: `python3 scripts/tier5-http-bench.py --lic-root "$LIC_ROOT"`.

Full org sweep: `LIC_ROOT=… ./scripts/run-full-benchmark-suite.sh` (never `SKIP_EXPLOITS=1` on merge-worthy httpd PRs).

## 2. Fill the comparison table

Read and update (auto-generated, commit when changed):

- `docs/ecosystem/http-server-rps-matrix.md`
- `data/latest/benchmark-matrix.md` (HTTP sections)

**Every scenario** from `vendor/lis-tier5/benchmarks/tier5_http/suite.toml` must appear:

| RPS | `static_small`, `keepalive_pipelining`, `static_large`, `proxy_loopback`, `lb_round_robin`, `lb_least_conn`, `lb_peer_down` |
| Verify | `rate_limit_429`, `https_static` |

**Columns (RPS rows):** `li`, `nginx`, `apache`, `lighttpd`, `node`, `bun`, `li/nginx`.

- **`li` must be present on every row** — use measured RPS, `FAIL` (harness `wrk_parse_fail_li`), or `—` with **Li notes** in the matrix when blocked.
- Do not drop proxy/LB rows because only nginx has data today.

## 3. PR / release notes

- Paste the **HTTP performance (RPS)** table into the PR body.
- `CHANGELOG.md` + `docs/release-notes/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` with before/after RPS for touched scenarios.
- New capability → add scenario per [http-server-benchmark-growth.md](../../docs/ecosystem/http-server-benchmark-growth.md).

## 4. Do not

- Tune gates on `lic` `main` stub alone without epoll `LIC_ROOT` (see [lic-httpd-bench-compat.md](../../docs/ecosystem/lic-httpd-bench-compat.md)).
- Copy `li_rt_net.c` into **benchmarks**.
- Merge httpd perf without re-running the matrix on the same `LIC_ROOT` commit you ship.
